      "Language": "eng",
      "Abstract": {"AbstractText": "The role of allergic rhinitis (AR) in the development of chronic rhinosinusitis (CRS) in children remains unknown. This study demonstrates the degree of atopy, as reflected by the number of aeroallergen sensitivities or the presence of atopic comorbidities, is not associated with progression to CRS in the pediatric age group."},
